{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc 'nl -ba pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegation_release.go'","aggregated_output":"     1\tpackage pose\n     2\t\n     3\t// Releasing an abandoned attempt (spec\n     4\t// pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes R5): a dispatch that\n     5\t// ends after reserving its attempt but before recording its run leaves a\n     6\t// reservation without a receipt. Every later dispatch of the bundle refuses\n     7\t// on it, and cancellation refused it because nothing runs. Once it is proven\n     8\t// abandoned, the attempt is closed by the same records a failed run writes:\n     9\t// a failed run naming the abandonment and its receipt. Nothing is deleted\n    10\t// from the ledger.\n    11\t//\n    12\t// Proof of abandonment: a marker that is stalled with its owner proven dead;\n    13\t// or, for a reservation an earlier engine left without any marker (it\n    14\t// reserved before marking), no marker, no receipt, no run of the attempt and\n    15\t// a reservation older than reviewOrphanReservationAge, far beyond the\n    16\t// instant an earlier engine took between reserving and marking (review\n    17\t// round 2, N1). One release runs at a time per attempt: a claim published\n    18\t// exclusively guards it (N3).\n    19\t\n    20\timport (\n    21\t\t\"errors\"\n    22\t\t\"fmt\"\n    23\t\t\"os\"\n    24\t\t\"path/filepath\"\n    25\t\t\"strings\"\n    26\t\t\"time\"\n    27\t)\n    28\t\n    29\t// ErrAttemptNotAbandoned means the attempt is running, finished, or not\n    30\t// proven abandoned.\n    31\tvar ErrAttemptNotAbandoned = errors.New(\"pose: the attempt is not an abandoned reservation\")\n    32\t\n    33\t// reviewOrphanReservationAge is how old a reservation without any marker\n    34\t// must be to count as abandoned.\n    35\tconst reviewOrphanReservationAge = 10 * time.Minute\n    36\t\n    37\t// ReleaseAbandonedAttempt records the failed run of an attempt whose\n    38\t// dispatch ended before recording it, and removes its stalled marker. A\n    39\t// stalled marker whose reservation was never published is only removed; the\n    40\t// returned run is then empty.\n    41\tfunc (s Store) ReleaseAbandonedAttempt(attemptID string, now time.Time) (ReviewRun, error) {\n    42\t\tif !validAttemptFileName(attemptID) {\n    43\t\t\treturn ReviewRun{}, fmt.Errorf(\"%w: %q names no attempt\", ErrAttemptNotAbandoned, attemptID)\n    44\t\t}\n    45\t\tmarkers, _, err := s.ListDelegationActive()\n    46\t\tif err != nil {\n    47\t\t\treturn ReviewRun{}, err\n    48\t\t}\n    49\t\tvar marker *DelegationActiveRun\n    50\t\tfor i := range markers {\n    51\t\t\tif markers[i].AttemptID == attemptID {\n    52\t\t\t\tmarker = &markers[i]\n    53\t\t\t}\n    54\t\t}\n    55\t\tif marker != nil && (marker.StalledAt == \"\" || marker.Liveness != LockOwnerDead) {\n    56\t\t\treturn ReviewRun{}, fmt.Errorf(\"%w: its owner is not proven gone\", ErrAttemptNotAbandoned)\n    57\t\t}\n    58\t\tdir, err := s.delegationActiveDir(true)\n    59\t\tif err != nil {\n    60\t\t\treturn ReviewRun{}, err\n    61\t\t}\n    62\t\tclaim := filepath.Join(dir, attemptID+\".release\")\n    63\t\tif err := PublishFile(claim, []byte(now.UTC().Format(time.RFC3339Nano)+\"\\n\"), 0600, PublishAuthoritative, PublishExpectation{Mode: ExpectAbsent}); err != nil {\n    64\t\t\treturn ReviewRun{}, fmt.Errorf(\"%w: another release of it is in progress or was interrupted (%s)\", ErrAttemptNotAbandoned, claim)\n    65\t\t}\n    66\t\trun, err := s.releaseAbandonedAttemptClaimed(attemptID, marker, now)\n    67\t\tif rerr := os.Remove(claim); rerr != nil && !errors.Is(rerr, os.ErrNotExist) && err == nil {\n    68\t\t\terr = rerr\n    69\t\t}\n    70\t\treturn run, err\n    71\t}\n    72\t\n    73\tfunc (s Store) releaseAbandonedAttemptClaimed(attemptID string, marker *DelegationActiveRun, now time.Time) (ReviewRun, error) {\n    74\t\tvar reserved *DelegatedReviewAttempt\n    75\t\tif marker != nil {\n    76\t\t\tattempts, err := s.readDelegatedReviewAttempts(marker.BundleID)\n    77\t\t\tif err != nil {\n    78\t\t\t\treturn ReviewRun{}, err\n    79\t\t\t}\n    80\t\t\tfor i := range attempts {\n    81\t\t\t\tif attempts[i].AttemptID == attemptID {\n    82\t\t\t\t\treserved = &attempts[i]\n    83\t\t\t\t}\n    84\t\t\t}\n    85\t\t\tif reserved == nil {\n    86\t\t\t\t// The dispatch ended between its marker and its reservation:\n    87\t\t\t\t// nothing blocks the bundle, and the marker alone is removed.\n    88\t\t\t\treturn ReviewRun{}, s.removeDelegationMarker(*marker)\n    89\t\t\t}\n    90\t\t} else {\n    91\t\t\torphans, err := s.orphanReservations(now)\n    92\t\t\tif err != nil {\n    93\t\t\t\treturn ReviewRun{}, err\n    94\t\t\t}\n    95\t\t\tfor i := range orphans {\n    96\t\t\t\tif orphans[i].AttemptID == attemptID {\n    97\t\t\t\t\treserved = &orphans[i]\n    98\t\t\t\t}\n    99\t\t\t}\n   100\t\t\tif reserved == nil {\n   101\t\t\t\treturn ReviewRun{}, fmt.Errorf(\"%w: no stalled marker and no reservation older than %s without a receipt\", ErrAttemptNotAbandoned, reviewOrphanReservationAge)\n   102\t\t\t}\n   103\t\t}\n   104\t\tif _, err := os.Lstat(attemptReceiptPath(s.Root, *reserved)); err == nil {\n   105\t\t\treturn ReviewRun{}, fmt.Errorf(\"%w: it already has a receipt\", ErrAttemptNotAbandoned)\n   106\t\t} else if !errors.Is(err, os.ErrNotExist) {\n   107\t\t\treturn ReviewRun{}, fmt.Errorf(\"the receipt of %s cannot be inspected: %w\", attemptID, err)\n   108\t\t}\n   109\t\trun := ReviewRun{SchemaVersion: 1, Scope: reserved.Scope, BundleID: reserved.BundleID, BundleDigest: reserved.BundleDigest,\n   110\t\t\tKind: ReviewBriefKindReview, Adapter: reserved.Adapter, Reason: reserved.Reason, AttemptID: reserved.AttemptID,\n   111\t\t\tStartedAt: reserved.ReservedAt, ExitCode: -1, Purpose: DelegationPurposeReview,\n   112\t\t\tStatus: ReviewRunFailed, EndedAt: now.UTC().Format(time.RFC3339Nano)}\n   113\t\tif marker != nil {\n   114\t\t\trun.Kind, run.Purpose, run.Label, run.Round, run.StartedAt = DelegationKindForPurpose(marker.Purpose), marker.Purpose, marker.Label, marker.Round, marker.StartedAt\n   115\t\t\trun.Failure = DelegationAbandonedCause + \" (stalled at \" + marker.StalledAt + \"); released by pose delegate cancel\"\n   116\t\t} else {\n   117\t\t\trun.Failure = DelegationAbandonedCause + \" (reservation of \" + reserved.ReservedAt + \" with no marker, left by an earlier engine); released by pose delegate cancel\"\n   118\t\t}\n   119\t\trecorded, err := s.recordReviewRun(run, nil)\n   120\t\tif err != nil {\n   121\t\t\treturn ReviewRun{}, err\n   122\t\t}\n   123\t\tif err := s.finishDelegatedReviewAttempt(*reserved, recorded); err != nil {\n   124\t\t\treturn recorded, err\n   125\t\t}\n   126\t\tif marker != nil {\n   127\t\t\treturn recorded, s.removeDelegationMarker(*marker)\n   128\t\t}\n   129\t\treturn recorded, nil\n   130\t}\n   131\t\n   132\t// orphanReservations lists the reservations an earlier engine left without\n   133\t// a receipt, a marker or a run, older than reviewOrphanReservationAge.\n   134\tfunc (s Store) orphanReservations(now time.Time) ([]DelegatedReviewAttempt, error) {\n   135\t\tbase := filepath.Join(s.Root, reviewAttemptDir)\n   136\t\tdirs, err := os.ReadDir(base)\n   137\t\tif errors.Is(err, os.ErrNotExist) {\n   138\t\t\treturn nil, nil\n   139\t\t}\n   140\t\tif err != nil {\n   141\t\t\treturn nil, err\n   142\t\t}\n   143\t\tmarkers, _, err := s.ListDelegationActive()\n   144\t\tif err != nil {\n   145\t\t\treturn nil, err\n   146\t\t}\n   147\t\tmarked := map[string]bool{}\n   148\t\tfor _, m := range markers {\n   149\t\t\tmarked[m.AttemptID] = true\n   150\t\t}\n   151\t\truns, _, err := s.ReadReviewRuns(\"\")\n   152\t\tif err != nil {\n   153\t\t\treturn nil, err\n   154\t\t}\n   155\t\tran := map[string]bool{}\n   156\t\tfor _, r := range runs {\n   157\t\t\tran[r.AttemptID] = true\n   158\t\t}\n   159\t\tvar out []DelegatedReviewAttempt\n   160\t\tbudget := reviewReadBudget(nil)\n   161\t\tfor _, d := range dirs {\n   162\t\t\tif !d.IsDir() {\n   163\t\t\t\tcontinue\n   164\t\t\t}\n   165\t\t\tentries, err := os.ReadDir(filepath.Join(base, d.Name()))\n   166\t\t\tif err != nil {\n   167\t\t\t\treturn nil, err\n   168\t\t\t}\n   169\t\t\tfor _, e := range entries {\n   170\t\t\t\tif IsPublisherStaging(e.Name()) || !strings.HasSuffix(e.Name(), \".json\") || strings.HasSuffix(e.Name(), \".result.json\") {\n   171\t\t\t\t\tcontinue\n   172\t\t\t\t}\n   173\t\t\t\tvar a DelegatedReviewAttempt\n   174\t\t\t\tif err := readLedgerJSONBudgetIn(s.fsys(), filepath.Join(base, d.Name(), e.Name()), &a, budget); err != nil || a.AttemptID != attemptIdentity(a) {\n   175\t\t\t\t\tcontinue\n   176\t\t\t\t}\n   177\t\t\t\tif marked[a.AttemptID] || ran[a.AttemptID] {\n   178\t\t\t\t\tcontinue\n   179\t\t\t\t}\n   180\t\t\t\tif _, err := os.Lstat(attemptReceiptPath(s.Root, a)); !errors.Is(err, os.ErrNotExist) {\n   181\t\t\t\t\tcontinue\n   182\t\t\t\t}\n   183\t\t\t\tat, err := time.Parse(time.RFC3339Nano, a.ReservedAt)\n   184\t\t\t\tif err != nil || now.Sub(at) < reviewOrphanReservationAge {\n   185\t\t\t\t\tcontinue\n   186\t\t\t\t}\n   187\t\t\t\tout = append(out, a)\n   188\t\t\t}\n   189\t\t}\n   190\t\treturn out, nil\n   191\t}\n   192\t\n   193\tfunc (s Store) removeDelegationMarker(marker DelegationActiveRun) error {\n   194\t\tdir, err := s.delegationActiveDir(false)\n   195\t\tif err != nil {\n   196\t\t\treturn err\n   197\t\t}\n   198\t\tfor _, p := range []string{filepath.Join(dir, marker.AttemptID+\".json\"), stallClaimPath(dir, marker), cancelRequestPath(dir, marker)} {\n   199\t\t\tif err := os.Remove(p); err != nil && !errors.Is(err, os.ErrNotExist) {\n   200\t\t\t\treturn err\n   201\t\t\t}\n   202\t\t}\n   203\t\treturn nil\n   204\t}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"nl -ba .pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes.md | sed -n '20,100p;120,180p'\"","aggregated_output":"    20\t### Goal\n    21\tKeep a delegated review run concludable when the reviewer ends while a process it started is still running, by terminating and reaping the run's remaining processes before the cleanup inventory.\n    22\t\n    23\t### Business value\n    24\tRound 2 of `pose-review-readiness-before-seal` (rrn-9d5816c780952f13) produced a complete draft with two valid findings, but its cleanup was `runtime cleanup inventory incomplete; resources retained` because a broad `go test` the reviewer started was still running. The run could not be concluded and its findings had to be carried by hand. On 2026-11-24 a dispatch stopped during setup left reservation `000002.json` of attempt `rat-cfa14ceb…` with no run: every later dispatch failed with `attempt … incomplete or unreadable`, and `pose delegate cancel` refused it as `stalled, not running`; the reservation had to be moved out of the repository by hand.\n    25\t\n    26\t### Constraints\n    27\tCleanup keeps proving that the sealed checkout is unchanged and that no owned resource survives; only the order changes. A run whose resources truly cannot be reclaimed stays unconcludable.\n    28\t\n    29\t### Non-goals\n    30\tChanging review independence, round accounting or the attestation preflight.\n    31\t\n    32\t## 2. Requirements\n    33\t\n    34\t### Functional\n    35\t- R1: When the adapter exits, the dispatch shall terminate every remaining process of the run's process group, wait for them within a bound, and only then take the cleanup inventory.\n    36\t- R2: A run whose leftover processes were terminated and reaped, and whose inventory then completes, shall be concludable; the run record shall say which processes were terminated.\n    37\t- R3: The review brief shall ask the reviewer to let every command it starts finish before ending.\n    38\t- R4: A regression test shall dispatch an adapter that leaves a background process running and conclude the run.\n    39\t- R5: An attempt reservation whose dispatch was interrupted before its run was recorded shall not block later dispatches: `pose delegate ls` shall show it as abandoned with its cause, and `pose delegate cancel` (or the next dispatch) shall release it with a record, never by deleting the reservation.\n    40\t- R6: A regression test shall interrupt a dispatch between the reservation and the run record and dispatch again.\n    41\t\n    42\t### Non-functional\n    43\tExisting behaviour outside the stated requirements is unchanged.\n    44\t\n    45\t### Security\n    46\tNo new input crosses a trust boundary without the existing confinement.\n    47\t\n    48\t### Compatibility\n    49\tRecords written by earlier engines keep their meaning.\n    50\t\n    51\t## 3. Technical Plan\n    52\t\n    53\t### Affected areas\n    54\t`pose-mcp` (review dispatch and conclusion), the manual and its embedded copy.\n    55\t\n    56\t### Artifacts\n    57\t- created: .pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes.md\n    58\t- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_reap_linux.go\n    59\t- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_reap_other.go\n    60\t- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_reap_linux_test.go\n    61\t- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegation_list.go\n    62\t- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegation_release.go\n    63\t- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegation_release_test.go\n    64\t- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go\n    65\t- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_attempt_ledger.go\n    66\t- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_adapter_containment.go\n    67\t- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_adapter_containment_regression_test.go\n    68\t- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief.go\n    69\t- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief_test.go\n    70\t- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief_conclusion_rules_test.go\n    71\t- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/testdata/review_brief_template_digests.json\n    72\t- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate.go\n    73\t- created: pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_reap_test.go\n    74\t- modified: POSE.md\n    75\t- modified: locales/pt-BR/POSE.md\n    76\t- modified: pose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/POSE.md\n    77\t- modified: pose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/locales/pt-BR/POSE.md\n    78\t\n    79\t\n    80\t### Delivery targets\n    81\t\n    82\t- capability:review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes module:pose-mcp profile:composed-capability entrypoint:pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate.go\n    83\t\n    84\t\n    85\t### API/contract changes\n    86\t`pose delegate cancel` releases a stalled attempt that has no run, recording a failed run and its receipt. Brief template `review-brief/10`. The run record's `safety.limitations` names the processes the dispatch ended after the adapter.\n    87\t\n    88\t\n    89\t### Data/storage changes\n    90\tA released attempt gets an ordinary failed run record and attempt receipt; no schema changes.\n    91\t\n    92\t\n    93\t### Technical risks\n    94\tThe leftover processes are found by the `POSE_SEALED_CHECKOUT=<checkout>` entry of their environment, which every process of the run inherits; a process that clears its environment escapes, and the existing cleanup inventory still fails that run (L1). Reading another process's environment needs Linux and the same user; elsewhere the group kill stays the only termination (L2).\n    95\t\n    96\t\n    97\t## 4. Tasks\n    98\t\n    99\t### Planning\n   100\t- [ ] Confirm the cause against the current engine before starting.\n   120\t### Strategy\n   121\tEach requirement gets a regression test shown failing before its code.\n   122\t\n   123\t### Deterministic checks\n   124\t\n   125\t#### Test\n   126\t- Command: `go test ./...` (in `pose-mcp`), then `pose validate --carry`.\n   127\t\n   128\t### Execution log\n   129\t- 2026-11-24: implemented R1–R6. Each has a test that fails with its fix mutated out: the dispatch ends a process the adapter left in a session of its own (the test's leftover keeps writing into the runtime directory), the release records the failed run and receipt and removes the marker and its stall claim, a live owner is never released, and `review-brief/10` asks commands to finish while `/9` stays unchanged.\n   130\t- 2026-11-24: the containment record disclosed escaped-descendant termination as `unavailable`, and a regression test pinned that limitation. On Linux it is now `environment-marked` (ended while the descendant keeps the run's sealed-checkout entry, never `available`, so a profile that requires the full guarantee is still refused), the limitation text says so, and the test now proves the escaped child is ended with the run.\n   131\t- 2026-11-24: review round 1 (rrn-c5c082703d83c834) requested changes. N1: the reservation was published before the active marker, so a dispatch ended in between left an attempt nothing could release; the dispatch now marks the attempt active first and publishes the reservation after, and a stalled marker without a reservation is removed by the release. When marking itself fails, the dispatch still publishes the reservation and records the failed run and its receipt, keeping the contract of `pose-delegation-result-before-marker`. N2: `delegate ls` now names the abandonment cause and the release command, in text and JSON. N3: each process is pinned by a pidfd and its environment read again through it before SIGKILL, so a reused pid is never signalled. N4: a scan that cannot list `/proc` or read a process state fails; a process of this user whose environment cannot be read is counted and disclosed in the run record rather than skipped (L3). N5: the manual says the reaping is Linux-only. Each fix has a test that fails with it mutated out (N4's disclosure is not reproducible in a test: it needs a non-inspectable process).\n   132\t- 2026-11-24: review round 2 (rrn-2c9fa8ac47c2fbab) requested changes. N1: a reservation an earlier engine left without any marker is now listed by `delegate ls` and released by `cancel` once it has no marker, receipt or run and is older than ten minutes (an earlier engine marked within moments of reserving). N2: a non-inspectable process of this user that did not exist before the adapter started may be the run's, so the scan fails and the run stays unconcludable; ones that predate the run are skipped and disclosed. N3: a release claims the attempt exclusively, so two cancels never record two runs. N4: `TestAnInterruptedDispatchIsReleasedAndTheNextOneRuns` interrupts a real dispatch after its reservation, sees the next dispatch refused with the release command, releases it and dispatches again. N5: a receipt that cannot be inspected is reported with its error. Each fix has a test that fails with it mutated out, except N5.\n   133\t\n   134\t\n   135\t### Results summary\n   136\tThe full `pose-mcp` suite passes; the canonical result is refreshed with `pose validate --carry`.\n   137\t\n   138\t\n   139\t### Requirement trace\n   140\t- R1 [satisfied] test:TestDispatchEndsWhatTheReviewerLeftRunning, test:TestAPidThatLostTheRunsEntryIsNotKilled, test:TestANonInspectableProcessStartedDuringTheRunFailsTheScan\n   141\t- R2 [satisfied] test:TestDispatchEndsWhatTheReviewerLeftRunning\n   142\t- R3 [satisfied] test:TestTheCurrentBriefAsksCommandsToFinish\n   143\t- R4 [satisfied] test:TestDispatchEndsWhatTheReviewerLeftRunning\n   144\t- R5 [satisfied] test:TestAnAbandonedAttemptIsReleasedWithARecord, test:TestTheAttemptIsMarkedActiveBeforeItIsReserved, test:TestAStalledMarkerWithoutReservationIsListedAndRemoved\n   145\t- R6 [satisfied] test:TestAnInterruptedDispatchIsReleasedAndTheNextOneRuns, test:TestAMarkerlessReservationOfAnEarlierEngineIsReleased, test:TestAClaimedReleaseIsNotRunTwice\n   146\t\n   147\t\n   148\t### Known gaps\n   149\tThe release is driven through the Store, including after a real interrupted dispatch; the thin `pose delegate cancel` branch that calls it is not driven through the CLI, because a stalled marker there needs a dispatch process killed and three silent heartbeat intervals. N5 (the receipt inspection error) has no test: making the receipt path uninspectable also makes the reservation unreadable first.\n   150\t\n   151\t\n   152\t## 7. Final Report\n   153\t\n   154\t### Delivered scope\n   155\tThe dispatch ends the processes a run left running before its cleanup and names them in the run record; `pose delegate cancel` releases an attempt abandoned before its run was recorded; `review-brief/10` asks the reviewer to let its commands finish.\n   156\t\n   157\t\n   158\t### Files and modules changed\n   159\t`pose-mcp` (review dispatch, attempt ledger, delegation CLI, brief), the manual in both locales and its embedded copies.\n   160\t\n   161\t\n   162\t### Validation executed\n   163\t`go test ./...` in `pose-mcp`; `pose check --strict`; `pose validate --carry --json-out .pose/results/delivery-validation.json`.\n   164\t\n   165\t\n   166\t### Residual risks\n   167\tL1: a process that clears its environment is not found; the cleanup inventory still fails that run. L2: outside Linux only the process-group kill applies. L3: a process of this user that made itself non-inspectable cannot be matched: one that predates the run is skipped and counted in the run record, and one started during the run fails the cleanup, so such a run is not concludable.\n   168\t\n   169\t\n   170\t### Follow-ups\n   171\tNone.\n   172\t\n   173\t\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
