{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_41","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"nl -ba .pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes.md | sed -n '20,180p'; nl -ba pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegation_release.go | sed -n '1,225p'; nl -ba pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegation_list.go | sed -n '65,220p'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_41","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"nl -ba .pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes.md | sed -n '20,180p'; nl -ba pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegation_release.go | sed -n '1,225p'; nl -ba pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegation_list.go | sed -n '65,220p'\"","aggregated_output":"    20\t### Goal\n    21\tKeep a delegated review run concludable when the reviewer ends while a process it started is still running, by terminating and reaping the run's remaining processes before the cleanup inventory.\n    22\t\n    23\t### Business value\n    24\tRound 2 of `pose-review-readiness-before-seal` (rrn-9d5816c780952f13) produced a complete draft with two valid findings, but its cleanup was `runtime cleanup inventory incomplete; resources retained` because a broad `go test` the reviewer started was still running. The run could not be concluded and its findings had to be carried by hand. On 2026-11-24 a dispatch stopped during setup left reservation `000002.json` of attempt `rat-cfa14ceb…` with no run: every later dispatch failed with `attempt … incomplete or unreadable`, and `pose delegate cancel` refused it as `stalled, not running`; the reservation had to be moved out of the repository by hand.\n    25\t\n    26\t### Constraints\n    27\tCleanup keeps proving that the sealed checkout is unchanged and that no owned resource survives; only the order changes. A run whose resources truly cannot be reclaimed stays unconcludable.\n    28\t\n    29\t### Non-goals\n    30\tChanging review independence, round accounting or the attestation preflight.\n    31\t\n    32\t## 2. Requirements\n    33\t\n    34\t### Functional\n    35\t- R1: When the adapter exits, the dispatch shall terminate every remaining process of the run's process group, wait for them within a bound, and only then take the cleanup inventory.\n    36\t- R2: A run whose leftover processes were terminated and reaped, and whose inventory then completes, shall be concludable; the run record shall say which processes were terminated.\n    37\t- R3: The review brief shall ask the reviewer to let every command it starts finish before ending.\n    38\t- R4: A regression test shall dispatch an adapter that leaves a background process running and conclude the run.\n    39\t- R5: An attempt reservation whose dispatch was interrupted before its run was recorded shall not block later dispatches: `pose delegate ls` shall show it as abandoned with its cause, and `pose delegate cancel` (or the next dispatch) shall release it with a record, never by deleting the reservation.\n    40\t- R6: A regression test shall interrupt a dispatch between the reservation and the run record and dispatch again.\n    41\t\n    42\t### Non-functional\n    43\tExisting behaviour outside the stated requirements is unchanged.\n    44\t\n    45\t### Security\n    46\tNo new input crosses a trust boundary without the existing confinement.\n    47\t\n    48\t### Compatibility\n    49\tRecords written by earlier engines keep their meaning.\n    50\t\n    51\t## 3. Technical Plan\n    52\t\n    53\t### Affected areas\n    54\t`pose-mcp` (review dispatch and conclusion), the manual and its embedded copy.\n    55\t\n    56\t### Artifacts\n    57\t- created: .pose/specs/2026-11-23-pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes.md\n    58\t- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_reap_linux.go\n    59\t- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_reap_other.go\n    60\t- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_reap_linux_test.go\n    61\t- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegation_list.go\n    62\t- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegation_release.go\n    63\t- created: pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegation_release_test.go\n    64\t- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go\n    65\t- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_attempt_ledger.go\n    66\t- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_adapter_containment.go\n    67\t- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_adapter_containment_regression_test.go\n    68\t- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief.go\n    69\t- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief_test.go\n    70\t- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief_conclusion_rules_test.go\n    71\t- modified: pose-mcp/internal/pose/testdata/review_brief_template_digests.json\n    72\t- modified: pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate.go\n    73\t- created: pose-mcp/internal/cli/review_reap_test.go\n    74\t- modified: POSE.md\n    75\t- modified: locales/pt-BR/POSE.md\n    76\t- modified: pose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/POSE.md\n    77\t- modified: pose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/locales/pt-BR/POSE.md\n    78\t\n    79\t\n    80\t### Delivery targets\n    81\t\n    82\t- capability:review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes module:pose-mcp profile:composed-capability entrypoint:pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate.go\n    83\t\n    84\t\n    85\t### API/contract changes\n    86\t`pose delegate cancel` releases a stalled attempt that has no run, recording a failed run and its receipt. Brief template `review-brief/10`. The run record's `safety.limitations` names the processes the dispatch ended after the adapter.\n    87\t\n    88\t\n    89\t### Data/storage changes\n    90\tA released attempt gets an ordinary failed run record and attempt receipt; no schema changes.\n    91\t\n    92\t\n    93\t### Technical risks\n    94\tThe leftover processes are found by the `POSE_SEALED_CHECKOUT=<checkout>` entry of their environment, which every process of the run inherits; a process that clears its environment escapes, and the existing cleanup inventory still fails that run (L1). Reading another process's environment needs Linux and the same user; elsewhere the group kill stays the only termination (L2).\n    95\t\n    96\t\n    97\t## 4. Tasks\n    98\t\n    99\t### Planning\n   100\t- [ ] Confirm the cause against the current engine before starting.\n   101\t\n   102\t### Implementation\n   103\t- [ ] Implement each requirement with a test that fails before it.\n   104\t\n   105\t### Validation\n   106\t- [ ] `pose validate --carry` and `pose check --strict`.\n   107\t\n   108\t## 5. Decisions\n   109\t\n   110\t### Decision D1\n   111\t- Basis: R1, R2\n   112\tLeftover processes are identified by the sealed-checkout entry the dispatch already sets in the run's environment, not by process group or session: adapters such as `codex exec` run each command in a session of its own, which the group kill misses, and the entry names this run's checkout only.\n   113\t\n   114\t### Decision D2\n   115\t- Basis: R5\n   116\tAn abandoned attempt is closed by the records a failed run writes (a run record and its receipt), released only when its marker is stalled and its owner proven dead. Nothing is deleted from the ledger, and older engines read the result as an ordinary failed run.\n   117\t\n   118\t## 6. Validation\n   119\t\n   120\t### Strategy\n   121\tEach requirement gets a regression test shown failing before its code.\n   122\t\n   123\t### Deterministic checks\n   124\t\n   125\t#### Test\n   126\t- Command: `go test ./...` (in `pose-mcp`), then `pose validate --carry`.\n   127\t\n   128\t### Execution log\n   129\t- 2026-11-24: implemented R1–R6. Each has a test that fails with its fix mutated out: the dispatch ends a process the adapter left in a session of its own (the test's leftover keeps writing into the runtime directory), the release records the failed run and receipt and removes the marker and its stall claim, a live owner is never released, and `review-brief/10` asks commands to finish while `/9` stays unchanged.\n   130\t- 2026-11-24: the containment record disclosed escaped-descendant termination as `unavailable`, and a regression test pinned that limitation. On Linux it is now `environment-marked` (ended while the descendant keeps the run's sealed-checkout entry, never `available`, so a profile that requires the full guarantee is still refused), the limitation text says so, and the test now proves the escaped child is ended with the run.\n   131\t- 2026-11-24: review round 1 (rrn-c5c082703d83c834) requested changes. N1: the reservation was published before the active marker, so a dispatch ended in between left an attempt nothing could release; the dispatch now marks the attempt active first and publishes the reservation after, and a stalled marker without a reservation is removed by the release. When marking itself fails, the dispatch still publishes the reservation and records the failed run and its receipt, keeping the contract of `pose-delegation-result-before-marker`. N2: `delegate ls` now names the abandonment cause and the release command, in text and JSON. N3: each process is pinned by a pidfd and its environment read again through it before SIGKILL, so a reused pid is never signalled. N4: a scan that cannot list `/proc` or read a process state fails; a process of this user whose environment cannot be read is counted and disclosed in the run record rather than skipped (L3). N5: the manual says the reaping is Linux-only. Each fix has a test that fails with it mutated out (N4's disclosure is not reproducible in a test: it needs a non-inspectable process).\n   132\t- 2026-11-24: review round 2 (rrn-2c9fa8ac47c2fbab) requested changes. N1: a reservation an earlier engine left without any marker is now listed by `delegate ls` and released by `cancel` once it has no marker, receipt or run and is older than ten minutes (an earlier engine marked within moments of reserving). N2: a non-inspectable process of this user that did not exist before the adapter started may be the run's, so the scan fails and the run stays unconcludable; ones that predate the run are skipped and disclosed. N3: a release claims the attempt exclusively, so two cancels never record two runs. N4: `TestAnInterruptedDispatchIsReleasedAndTheNextOneRuns` interrupts a real dispatch after its reservation, sees the next dispatch refused with the release command, releases it and dispatches again. N5: a receipt that cannot be inspected is reported with its error. Each fix has a test that fails with it mutated out, except N5.\n   133\t\n   134\t\n   135\t### Results summary\n   136\tThe full `pose-mcp` suite passes; the canonical result is refreshed with `pose validate --carry`.\n   137\t\n   138\t\n   139\t### Requirement trace\n   140\t- R1 [satisfied] test:TestDispatchEndsWhatTheReviewerLeftRunning, test:TestAPidThatLostTheRunsEntryIsNotKilled, test:TestANonInspectableProcessStartedDuringTheRunFailsTheScan\n   141\t- R2 [satisfied] test:TestDispatchEndsWhatTheReviewerLeftRunning\n   142\t- R3 [satisfied] test:TestTheCurrentBriefAsksCommandsToFinish\n   143\t- R4 [satisfied] test:TestDispatchEndsWhatTheReviewerLeftRunning\n   144\t- R5 [satisfied] test:TestAnAbandonedAttemptIsReleasedWithARecord, test:TestTheAttemptIsMarkedActiveBeforeItIsReserved, test:TestAStalledMarkerWithoutReservationIsListedAndRemoved\n   145\t- R6 [satisfied] test:TestAnInterruptedDispatchIsReleasedAndTheNextOneRuns, test:TestAMarkerlessReservationOfAnEarlierEngineIsReleased, test:TestAClaimedReleaseIsNotRunTwice\n   146\t\n   147\t\n   148\t### Known gaps\n   149\tThe release is driven through the Store, including after a real interrupted dispatch; the thin `pose delegate cancel` branch that calls it is not driven through the CLI, because a stalled marker there needs a dispatch process killed and three silent heartbeat intervals. N5 (the receipt inspection error) has no test: making the receipt path uninspectable also makes the reservation unreadable first.\n   150\t\n   151\t\n   152\t## 7. Final Report\n   153\t\n   154\t### Delivered scope\n   155\tThe dispatch ends the processes a run left running before its cleanup and names them in the run record; `pose delegate cancel` releases an attempt abandoned before its run was recorded; `review-brief/10` asks the reviewer to let its commands finish.\n   156\t\n   157\t\n   158\t### Files and modules changed\n   159\t`pose-mcp` (review dispatch, attempt ledger, delegation CLI, brief), the manual in both locales and its embedded copies.\n   160\t\n   161\t\n   162\t### Validation executed\n   163\t`go test ./...` in `pose-mcp`; `pose check --strict`; `pose validate --carry --json-out .pose/results/delivery-validation.json`.\n   164\t\n   165\t\n   166\t### Residual risks\n   167\tL1: a process that clears its environment is not found; the cleanup inventory still fails that run. L2: outside Linux only the process-group kill applies. L3: a process of this user that made itself non-inspectable cannot be matched: one that predates the run is skipped and counted in the run record, and one started during the run fails the cleanup, so such a run is not concludable.\n   168\t\n   169\t\n   170\t### Follow-ups\n   171\tNone.\n   172\t\n   173\t\n     1\tpackage pose\n     2\t\n     3\t// Releasing an abandoned attempt (spec\n     4\t// pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes R5): a dispatch that\n     5\t// ends after reserving its attempt but before recording its run leaves a\n     6\t// reservation without a receipt. Every later dispatch of the bundle refuses\n     7\t// on it, and cancellation refused it because nothing runs. Once it is proven\n     8\t// abandoned, the attempt is closed by the same records a failed run writes:\n     9\t// a failed run naming the abandonment and its receipt. Nothing is deleted\n    10\t// from the ledger.\n    11\t//\n    12\t// Proof of abandonment: a marker that is stalled with its owner proven dead;\n    13\t// or, for a reservation an earlier engine left without any marker (it\n    14\t// reserved before marking), no marker, no receipt, no run of the attempt and\n    15\t// a reservation older than reviewOrphanReservationAge, far beyond the\n    16\t// instant an earlier engine took between reserving and marking (review\n    17\t// round 2, N1). One release runs at a time per attempt: a claim published\n    18\t// exclusively guards it (N3).\n    19\t\n    20\timport (\n    21\t\t\"errors\"\n    22\t\t\"fmt\"\n    23\t\t\"os\"\n    24\t\t\"path/filepath\"\n    25\t\t\"strings\"\n    26\t\t\"time\"\n    27\t)\n    28\t\n    29\t// ErrAttemptNotAbandoned means the attempt is running, finished, or not\n    30\t// proven abandoned.\n    31\tvar ErrAttemptNotAbandoned = errors.New(\"pose: the attempt is not an abandoned reservation\")\n    32\t\n    33\t// reviewOrphanReservationAge is how old a reservation without any marker\n    34\t// must be to count as abandoned.\n    35\tconst reviewOrphanReservationAge = 10 * time.Minute\n    36\t\n    37\t// ReleaseAbandonedAttempt records the failed run of an attempt whose\n    38\t// dispatch ended before recording it, and removes its stalled marker. A\n    39\t// stalled marker whose reservation was never published is only removed; the\n    40\t// returned run is then empty.\n    41\tfunc (s Store) ReleaseAbandonedAttempt(attemptID string, now time.Time) (ReviewRun, error) {\n    42\t\tif !validAttemptFileName(attemptID) {\n    43\t\t\treturn ReviewRun{}, fmt.Errorf(\"%w: %q names no attempt\", ErrAttemptNotAbandoned, attemptID)\n    44\t\t}\n    45\t\tmarkers, _, err := s.ListDelegationActive()\n    46\t\tif err != nil {\n    47\t\t\treturn ReviewRun{}, err\n    48\t\t}\n    49\t\tvar marker *DelegationActiveRun\n    50\t\tfor i := range markers {\n    51\t\t\tif markers[i].AttemptID == attemptID {\n    52\t\t\t\tmarker = &markers[i]\n    53\t\t\t}\n    54\t\t}\n    55\t\tif marker != nil && (marker.StalledAt == \"\" || marker.Liveness != LockOwnerDead) {\n    56\t\t\treturn ReviewRun{}, fmt.Errorf(\"%w: its owner is not proven gone\", ErrAttemptNotAbandoned)\n    57\t\t}\n    58\t\tdir, err := s.delegationActiveDir(true)\n    59\t\tif err != nil {\n    60\t\t\treturn ReviewRun{}, err\n    61\t\t}\n    62\t\tclaim := filepath.Join(dir, attemptID+\".release\")\n    63\t\tif err := PublishFile(claim, []byte(now.UTC().Format(time.RFC3339Nano)+\"\\n\"), 0600, PublishAuthoritative, PublishExpectation{Mode: ExpectAbsent}); err != nil {\n    64\t\t\treturn ReviewRun{}, fmt.Errorf(\"%w: another release of it is in progress or was interrupted (%s)\", ErrAttemptNotAbandoned, claim)\n    65\t\t}\n    66\t\trun, err := s.releaseAbandonedAttemptClaimed(attemptID, marker, now)\n    67\t\tif rerr := os.Remove(claim); rerr != nil && !errors.Is(rerr, os.ErrNotExist) && err == nil {\n    68\t\t\terr = rerr\n    69\t\t}\n    70\t\treturn run, err\n    71\t}\n    72\t\n    73\tfunc (s Store) releaseAbandonedAttemptClaimed(attemptID string, marker *DelegationActiveRun, now time.Time) (ReviewRun, error) {\n    74\t\tvar reserved *DelegatedReviewAttempt\n    75\t\tif marker != nil {\n    76\t\t\tattempts, err := s.readDelegatedReviewAttempts(marker.BundleID)\n    77\t\t\tif err != nil {\n    78\t\t\t\treturn ReviewRun{}, err\n    79\t\t\t}\n    80\t\t\tfor i := range attempts {\n    81\t\t\t\tif attempts[i].AttemptID == attemptID {\n    82\t\t\t\t\treserved = &attempts[i]\n    83\t\t\t\t}\n    84\t\t\t}\n    85\t\t\tif reserved == nil {\n    86\t\t\t\t// The dispatch ended between its marker and its reservation:\n    87\t\t\t\t// nothing blocks the bundle, and the marker alone is removed.\n    88\t\t\t\treturn ReviewRun{}, s.removeDelegationMarker(*marker)\n    89\t\t\t}\n    90\t\t} else {\n    91\t\t\torphans, err := s.orphanReservations(now)\n    92\t\t\tif err != nil {\n    93\t\t\t\treturn ReviewRun{}, err\n    94\t\t\t}\n    95\t\t\tfor i := range orphans {\n    96\t\t\t\tif orphans[i].AttemptID == attemptID {\n    97\t\t\t\t\treserved = &orphans[i]\n    98\t\t\t\t}\n    99\t\t\t}\n   100\t\t\tif reserved == nil {\n   101\t\t\t\treturn ReviewRun{}, fmt.Errorf(\"%w: no stalled marker and no reservation older than %s without a receipt\", ErrAttemptNotAbandoned, reviewOrphanReservationAge)\n   102\t\t\t}\n   103\t\t}\n   104\t\tif _, err := os.Lstat(attemptReceiptPath(s.Root, *reserved)); err == nil {\n   105\t\t\treturn ReviewRun{}, fmt.Errorf(\"%w: it already has a receipt\", ErrAttemptNotAbandoned)\n   106\t\t} else if !errors.Is(err, os.ErrNotExist) {\n   107\t\t\treturn ReviewRun{}, fmt.Errorf(\"the receipt of %s cannot be inspected: %w\", attemptID, err)\n   108\t\t}\n   109\t\trun := ReviewRun{SchemaVersion: 1, Scope: reserved.Scope, BundleID: reserved.BundleID, BundleDigest: reserved.BundleDigest,\n   110\t\t\tKind: ReviewBriefKindReview, Adapter: reserved.Adapter, Reason: reserved.Reason, AttemptID: reserved.AttemptID,\n   111\t\t\tStartedAt: reserved.ReservedAt, ExitCode: -1, Purpose: DelegationPurposeReview,\n   112\t\t\tStatus: ReviewRunFailed, EndedAt: now.UTC().Format(time.RFC3339Nano)}\n   113\t\tif marker != nil {\n   114\t\t\trun.Kind, run.Purpose, run.Label, run.Round, run.StartedAt = DelegationKindForPurpose(marker.Purpose), marker.Purpose, marker.Label, marker.Round, marker.StartedAt\n   115\t\t\trun.Failure = DelegationAbandonedCause + \" (stalled at \" + marker.StalledAt + \"); released by pose delegate cancel\"\n   116\t\t} else {\n   117\t\t\trun.Failure = DelegationAbandonedCause + \" (reservation of \" + reserved.ReservedAt + \" with no marker, left by an earlier engine); released by pose delegate cancel\"\n   118\t\t}\n   119\t\trecorded, err := s.recordReviewRun(run, nil)\n   120\t\tif err != nil {\n   121\t\t\treturn ReviewRun{}, err\n   122\t\t}\n   123\t\tif err := s.finishDelegatedReviewAttempt(*reserved, recorded); err != nil {\n   124\t\t\treturn recorded, err\n   125\t\t}\n   126\t\tif marker != nil {\n   127\t\t\treturn recorded, s.removeDelegationMarker(*marker)\n   128\t\t}\n   129\t\treturn recorded, nil\n   130\t}\n   131\t\n   132\t// orphanReservations lists the reservations an earlier engine left without\n   133\t// a receipt, a marker or a run, older than reviewOrphanReservationAge.\n   134\tfunc (s Store) orphanReservations(now time.Time) ([]DelegatedReviewAttempt, error) {\n   135\t\tbase := filepath.Join(s.Root, reviewAttemptDir)\n   136\t\tdirs, err := os.ReadDir(base)\n   137\t\tif errors.Is(err, os.ErrNotExist) {\n   138\t\t\treturn nil, nil\n   139\t\t}\n   140\t\tif err != nil {\n   141\t\t\treturn nil, err\n   142\t\t}\n   143\t\tmarkers, _, err := s.ListDelegationActive()\n   144\t\tif err != nil {\n   145\t\t\treturn nil, err\n   146\t\t}\n   147\t\tmarked := map[string]bool{}\n   148\t\tfor _, m := range markers {\n   149\t\t\tmarked[m.AttemptID] = true\n   150\t\t}\n   151\t\truns, _, err := s.ReadReviewRuns(\"\")\n   152\t\tif err != nil {\n   153\t\t\treturn nil, err\n   154\t\t}\n   155\t\tran := map[string]bool{}\n   156\t\tfor _, r := range runs {\n   157\t\t\tran[r.AttemptID] = true\n   158\t\t}\n   159\t\tvar out []DelegatedReviewAttempt\n   160\t\tbudget := reviewReadBudget(nil)\n   161\t\tfor _, d := range dirs {\n   162\t\t\tif !d.IsDir() {\n   163\t\t\t\tcontinue\n   164\t\t\t}\n   165\t\t\tentries, err := os.ReadDir(filepath.Join(base, d.Name()))\n   166\t\t\tif err != nil {\n   167\t\t\t\treturn nil, err\n   168\t\t\t}\n   169\t\t\tfor _, e := range entries {\n   170\t\t\t\tif IsPublisherStaging(e.Name()) || !strings.HasSuffix(e.Name(), \".json\") || strings.HasSuffix(e.Name(), \".result.json\") {\n   171\t\t\t\t\tcontinue\n   172\t\t\t\t}\n   173\t\t\t\tvar a DelegatedReviewAttempt\n   174\t\t\t\tif err := readLedgerJSONBudgetIn(s.fsys(), filepath.Join(base, d.Name(), e.Name()), &a, budget); err != nil || a.AttemptID != attemptIdentity(a) {\n   175\t\t\t\t\tcontinue\n   176\t\t\t\t}\n   177\t\t\t\tif marked[a.AttemptID] || ran[a.AttemptID] {\n   178\t\t\t\t\tcontinue\n   179\t\t\t\t}\n   180\t\t\t\tif _, err := os.Lstat(attemptReceiptPath(s.Root, a)); !errors.Is(err, os.ErrNotExist) {\n   181\t\t\t\t\tcontinue\n   182\t\t\t\t}\n   183\t\t\t\tat, err := time.Parse(time.RFC3339Nano, a.ReservedAt)\n   184\t\t\t\tif err != nil || now.Sub(at) < reviewOrphanReservationAge {\n   185\t\t\t\t\tcontinue\n   186\t\t\t\t}\n   187\t\t\t\tout = append(out, a)\n   188\t\t\t}\n   189\t\t}\n   190\t\treturn out, nil\n   191\t}\n   192\t\n   193\tfunc (s Store) removeDelegationMarker(marker DelegationActiveRun) error {\n   194\t\tdir, err := s.delegationActiveDir(false)\n   195\t\tif err != nil {\n   196\t\t\treturn err\n   197\t\t}\n   198\t\tfor _, p := range []string{filepath.Join(dir, marker.AttemptID+\".json\"), stallClaimPath(dir, marker), cancelRequestPath(dir, marker)} {\n   199\t\t\tif err := os.Remove(p); err != nil && !errors.Is(err, os.ErrNotExist) {\n   200\t\t\t\treturn err\n   201\t\t\t}\n   202\t\t}\n   203\t\treturn nil\n   204\t}\n    65\t\tDelegationStalled = \"stalled\"\n    66\t\t// DelegationAbandonedCause is the failure of a stalled attempt whose\n    67\t\t// dispatch ended before recording its run.\n    68\t\tDelegationAbandonedCause = \"abandoned: the dispatching process ended before the run was recorded\"\n    69\t)\n    70\t\n    71\t// ListDelegationAttempts groups every recorded run by attempt, adds the runs\n    72\t// in progress, and returns the losses the run history reports.\n    73\tfunc (s Store) ListDelegationAttempts() ([]DelegationAttempt, []string, error) {\n    74\t\t// The markers are read before the runs: a run publishes its record before\n    75\t\t// it removes its marker, so a reader that finds no marker for an attempt\n    76\t\t// it saw running finds its record (spec\n    77\t\t// pose-delegated-review-completion-signal R5).\n    78\t\tactive, activeLost, activeErr := s.ListDelegationActive()\n    79\t\truns, lost, err := s.ReadReviewRuns(\"\")\n    80\t\tif err != nil {\n    81\t\t\treturn nil, nil, err\n    82\t\t}\n    83\t\t// Task runs share the lifecycle, never the review history (spec\n    84\t\t// pose-delegation-task R7, R8).\n    85\t\ttasks, taskLost := s.ReadDelegationTaskRuns()\n    86\t\truns, lost = append(runs, tasks...), append(lost, taskLost...)\n    87\t\tbyAttempt := map[string]*DelegationAttempt{}\n    88\t\torder := []string{}\n    89\t\tfor i := range runs {\n    90\t\t\trun := runs[i]\n    91\t\t\tkey := run.AttemptID\n    92\t\t\tif key == \"\" {\n    93\t\t\t\tkey = run.RunID // a run recorded before attempts existed is its own attempt\n    94\t\t\t}\n    95\t\t\trow, ok := byAttempt[key]\n    96\t\t\tif !ok {\n    97\t\t\t\trow = &DelegationAttempt{AttemptID: key, StartedAt: run.StartedAt}\n    98\t\t\t\tbyAttempt[key] = row\n    99\t\t\t\torder = append(order, key)\n   100\t\t\t}\n   101\t\t\trow.Runs = append(row.Runs, run.RunID)\n   102\t\t\trow.latest = &runs[i]\n   103\t\t\tif run.SessionDigest != \"\" {\n   104\t\t\t\tif value, err := s.readReviewSession(run.SessionDigest); err == nil {\n   105\t\t\t\t\trow.sessions = append(row.sessions, value)\n   106\t\t\t\t}\n   107\t\t\t}\n   108\t\t\tevents, err := s.ReadDelegationEvents(run)\n   109\t\t\tif err != nil {\n   110\t\t\t\t// A turn count read from nothing would report a whole history.\n   111\t\t\t\tlost = append(lost, \"the events of run \"+run.RunID+\" could not be read: \"+err.Error())\n   112\t\t\t} else {\n   113\t\t\t\tfor _, e := range events {\n   114\t\t\t\t\tif e.Kind == DelegationEventTurn {\n   115\t\t\t\t\t\trow.Turns++\n   116\t\t\t\t\t}\n   117\t\t\t\t}\n   118\t\t\t\tif len(events) > 0 {\n   119\t\t\t\t\trow.LastStep = delegationStepText(events[len(events)-1])\n   120\t\t\t\t}\n   121\t\t\t}\n   122\t\t}\n   123\t\tfor _, key := range order {\n   124\t\t\trow := byAttempt[key]\n   125\t\t\tlatest := row.latest\n   126\t\t\trow.LatestRun, row.State, row.Agent, row.Vendor, row.Model = latest.RunID, latest.Status, latest.Adapter, latest.Vendor, latest.Model\n   127\t\t\trow.Label, row.Scope, row.BundleID, row.EndedAt, row.Failure, row.Interruption = latest.Label, latest.Scope, latest.BundleID, latest.EndedAt, latest.Failure, latest.Interruption\n   128\t\t\trow.Purpose, row.Lead, row.Access = latest.Purpose, latest.Lead, DelegationAccessRead\n   129\t\t\tif latest.Access != \"\" {\n   130\t\t\t\trow.Access = latest.Access\n   131\t\t\t}\n   132\t\t\trow.Round = latest.Round\n   133\t\t\tif hook := s.ReadDelegationHook(latest.RunID); hook != nil {\n   134\t\t\t\trow.HookFailure = hook.Failure\n   135\t\t\t}\n   136\t\t\tif row.Purpose == \"\" {\n   137\t\t\t\trow.Purpose = DelegationPurposeForKind(latest.Kind)\n   138\t\t\t}\n   139\t\t\tif latest.Status == ReviewRunInterrupted {\n   140\t\t\t\trow.Partial = strings.TrimSpace(latest.Output) != \"\"\n   141\t\t\t\tif latest.Interruption != nil && latest.Interruption.ResetAt != \"\" {\n   142\t\t\t\t\tif at, err := time.Parse(time.RFC3339Nano, latest.Interruption.ResetAt); err == nil {\n   143\t\t\t\t\t\tleft := time.Until(at)\n   144\t\t\t\t\t\tif left < 0 {\n   145\t\t\t\t\t\t\tleft = 0\n   146\t\t\t\t\t\t}\n   147\t\t\t\t\t\trow.TimeLeft = left.Round(time.Second).String()\n   148\t\t\t\t\t}\n   149\t\t\t\t}\n   150\t\t\t}\n   151\t\t}\n   152\t\tif activeErr != nil {\n   153\t\t\tlost = append(lost, \"active runs could not be read: \"+activeErr.Error())\n   154\t\t}\n   155\t\tlost = append(lost, activeLost...)\n   156\t\tfor _, marker := range active {\n   157\t\t\trow, ok := byAttempt[marker.AttemptID]\n   158\t\t\tif !ok {\n   159\t\t\t\trow = &DelegationAttempt{AttemptID: marker.AttemptID, Runs: []string{}, StartedAt: marker.StartedAt, Purpose: marker.Purpose, Access: DelegationAccessRead, Agent: marker.Agent, Label: marker.Label, Scope: marker.Scope, BundleID: marker.BundleID}\n   160\t\t\t\tbyAttempt[marker.AttemptID] = row\n   161\t\t\t\torder = append(order, marker.AttemptID)\n   162\t\t\t}\n   163\t\t\trow.State, row.Active, row.Liveness, row.CancelRequested = DelegationRunning, true, marker.Liveness, marker.CancelRequested\n   164\t\t\tif marker.Round > 0 {\n   165\t\t\t\trow.Round = marker.Round\n   166\t\t\t}\n   167\t\t\trow.EndedAt, row.Failure, row.Interruption, row.Partial, row.TimeLeft = \"\", \"\", nil, false, \"\"\n   168\t\t\tif beat, err := time.Parse(time.RFC3339Nano, marker.HeartbeatAt); err == nil {\n   169\t\t\t\trow.HeartbeatAge = time.Since(beat).Round(time.Second).String()\n   170\t\t\t}\n   171\t\t\tif marker.StalledAt != \"\" {\n   172\t\t\t\trow.State, row.Active, row.StalledAt = DelegationStalled, false, marker.StalledAt\n   173\t\t\t\tif row.LatestRun == \"\" {\n   174\t\t\t\t\t// The dispatch ended before recording its run: the cause and\n   175\t\t\t\t\t// the release are said, not left to inspection (review round\n   176\t\t\t\t\t// 1, N2).\n   177\t\t\t\t\trow.Failure = DelegationAbandonedCause + \"; release it with `pose delegate cancel \" + marker.AttemptID + \"`\"\n   178\t\t\t\t}\n   179\t\t\t}\n   180\t\t\t// A running run's progress comes from its live events (R12).\n   181\t\t\tif live, _, err := s.ReadDelegationLiveEvents(marker.AttemptID, 0); err == nil && len(live) > 0 {\n   182\t\t\t\tfor _, e := range live {\n   183\t\t\t\t\tif e.Kind == DelegationEventTurn {\n   184\t\t\t\t\t\trow.Turns++\n   185\t\t\t\t\t}\n   186\t\t\t\t}\n   187\t\t\t\trow.LastStep = delegationStepText(live[len(live)-1])\n   188\t\t\t}\n   189\t\t}\n   190\t\t// A reservation an earlier engine left without a marker or a run is\n   191\t\t// listed too, so it can be named and released (review round 2, N1).\n   192\t\tif orphans, err := s.orphanReservations(time.Now()); err != nil {\n   193\t\t\tlost = append(lost, \"abandoned reservations could not be read: \"+err.Error())\n   194\t\t} else {\n   195\t\t\tfor _, a := range orphans {\n   196\t\t\t\tif _, ok := byAttempt[a.AttemptID]; ok {\n   197\t\t\t\t\tcontinue\n   198\t\t\t\t}\n   199\t\t\t\tbyAttempt[a.AttemptID] = &DelegationAttempt{AttemptID: a.AttemptID, Runs: []string{}, StartedAt: a.ReservedAt, Purpose: DelegationPurposeReview, Access: DelegationAccessRead, Agent: a.Adapter, Scope: a.Scope, BundleID: a.BundleID,\n   200\t\t\t\t\tState: DelegationStalled, StalledAt: a.ReservedAt, Failure: DelegationAbandonedCause + \"; release it with `pose delegate cancel \" + a.AttemptID + \"`\"}\n   201\t\t\t\torder = append(order, a.AttemptID)\n   202\t\t\t}\n   203\t\t}\n   204\t\tout := make([]DelegationAttempt, 0, len(order))\n   205\t\tfor _, key := range order {\n   206\t\t\tout = append(out, *byAttempt[key])\n   207\t\t}\n   208\t\tsort.SliceStable(out, func(i, j int) bool { return out[i].StartedAt < out[j].StartedAt })\n   209\t\treturn out, lost, nil\n   210\t}\n   211\t\n   212\tfunc delegationStepText(e DelegationEvent) string {\n   213\t\ttext := strings.Join(strings.Fields(e.Text), \" \")\n   214\t\tif len(text) > 80 {\n   215\t\t\tcut := 77\n   216\t\t\tfor cut > 0 && !utf8RuneStart(text[cut]) {\n   217\t\t\t\tcut--\n   218\t\t\t}\n   219\t\t\ttext = text[:cut] + \"...\"\n   220\t\t}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_42","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"nl -ba pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_reap_linux.go | sed -n '1,245p'; nl -ba pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go | sed -n '995,1075p'; nl -ba pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegation_release_test.go | sed -n '185,285p'; nl -ba pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate.go | sed -n '1110,1155p'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_42","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"nl -ba pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_reap_linux.go | sed -n '1,245p'; nl -ba pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go | sed -n '995,1075p'; nl -ba pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegation_release_test.go | sed -n '185,285p'; nl -ba pose-mcp/internal/cli/delegate.go | sed -n '1110,1155p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t//go:build linux\n     2\t\n     3\tpackage pose\n     4\t\n     5\t// Leftover reviewer processes (spec\n     6\t// pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes R1): an adapter such as\n     7\t// `codex exec` runs each command in a session of its own, so killing the\n     8\t// adapter's process group misses a command the reviewer left running, and\n     9\t// that command keeps writing into the run's runtime directory while the\n    10\t// cleanup inventory reads it. Every process of the run inherits\n    11\t// SealedCheckoutEnv naming the run's checkout, so the dispatch finds them by\n    12\t// that entry, ends them and waits for them before the inventory.\n    13\t//\n    14\t// Each process is pinned by a pidfd before it is signalled, and its\n    15\t// environment is read again through the pinned process, so a pid reused by\n    16\t// an unrelated process between the scan and the signal is never killed\n    17\t// (review round 1, N3). A scan that cannot list or read the state of the\n    18\t// processes fails. A process of this user whose environment cannot be read\n    19\t// (one that made itself non-inspectable) cannot be matched: one that already\n    20\t// existed before the adapter started is not the run's and is skipped; any\n    21\t// other may be the run's, so the scan fails and the run stays unconcludable\n    22\t// (review round 2, N2).\n    23\t\n    24\timport (\n    25\t\t\"bytes\"\n    26\t\t\"errors\"\n    27\t\t\"fmt\"\n    28\t\t\"io/fs\"\n    29\t\t\"os\"\n    30\t\t\"path/filepath\"\n    31\t\t\"strconv\"\n    32\t\t\"strings\"\n    33\t\t\"syscall\"\n    34\t\t\"time\"\n    35\t\n    36\t\t\"golang.org/x/sys/unix\"\n    37\t)\n    38\t\n    39\tconst reviewReapWait = 5 * time.Second\n    40\t\n    41\t// reapSealedCheckoutProcesses ends every process whose environment names\n    42\t// worktree as its sealed checkout and returns a description of each. An\n    43\t// error means the run's processes could not be proven ended within the bound.\n    44\tfunc reapSealedCheckoutProcesses(worktree string, baseline map[int]string) ([]string, int, error) {\n    45\t\tif worktree == \"\" {\n    46\t\t\treturn nil, 0, nil\n    47\t\t}\n    48\t\tentry := []byte(SealedCheckoutEnv + \"=\" + worktree)\n    49\t\tvar reaped []string\n    50\t\tseen := map[int]bool{}\n    51\t\tdeadline := time.Now().Add(reviewReapWait)\n    52\t\tunreadable := 0\n    53\t\tfor {\n    54\t\t\talive, opaque, err := reviewMarkedProcesses(entry)\n    55\t\t\tif err != nil {\n    56\t\t\t\treturn reaped, len(opaque), err\n    57\t\t\t}\n    58\t\t\tunreadable = 0\n    59\t\t\tfor pid, start := range opaque {\n    60\t\t\t\tif baseline[pid] != start {\n    61\t\t\t\t\treturn reaped, len(opaque), fmt.Errorf(\"process %d of this user started during the run and cannot be inspected; it may be the run's and was not ended\", pid)\n    62\t\t\t\t}\n    63\t\t\t\tunreadable++\n    64\t\t\t}\n    65\t\t\tfor _, pid := range alive {\n    66\t\t\t\tif !seen[pid] {\n    67\t\t\t\t\tseen[pid] = true\n    68\t\t\t\t\treaped = append(reaped, fmt.Sprintf(\"%d %s\", pid, reviewProcessName(pid)))\n    69\t\t\t\t}\n    70\t\t\t\tif err := killPinnedMarkedProcess(pid, entry); err != nil {\n    71\t\t\t\t\treturn reaped, unreadable, err\n    72\t\t\t\t}\n    73\t\t\t}\n    74\t\t\tif len(alive) == 0 {\n    75\t\t\t\treturn reaped, unreadable, nil\n    76\t\t\t}\n    77\t\t\tif time.Now().After(deadline) {\n    78\t\t\t\treturn reaped, unreadable, fmt.Errorf(\"%d process(es) of the run could not be ended\", len(alive))\n    79\t\t\t}\n    80\t\t\ttime.Sleep(50 * time.Millisecond)\n    81\t\t}\n    82\t}\n    83\t\n    84\t// reviewMarkedProcesses lists the live processes whose environment holds\n    85\t// entry, and counts this user's processes whose environment could not be\n    86\t// read. A process that is gone is skipped.\n    87\tfunc reviewMarkedProcesses(entry []byte) ([]int, map[int]string, error) {\n    88\t\tdirs, err := os.ReadDir(\"/proc\")\n    89\t\tif err != nil {\n    90\t\t\treturn nil, nil, fmt.Errorf(\"the run's processes could not be listed: %w\", err)\n    91\t\t}\n    92\t\tunreadable := map[int]string{}\n    93\t\tself, uid := os.Getpid(), os.Getuid()\n    94\t\tvar out []int\n    95\t\tfor _, d := range dirs {\n    96\t\t\tpid, err := strconv.Atoi(d.Name())\n    97\t\t\tif err != nil || pid == self {\n    98\t\t\t\tcontinue\n    99\t\t\t}\n   100\t\t\tmarked, err := reviewProcessMarked(pid, entry)\n   101\t\t\tswitch {\n   102\t\t\tcase reviewProcessGoneErr(err):\n   103\t\t\t\tcontinue\n   104\t\t\tcase err != nil:\n   105\t\t\t\tif owner, oerr := reviewProcessOwner(pid); oerr == nil && owner != uid {\n   106\t\t\t\t\tcontinue // another user's process never inherits this run's environment\n   107\t\t\t\t} else if reviewProcessGoneErr(oerr) {\n   108\t\t\t\t\tcontinue\n   109\t\t\t\t}\n   110\t\t\t\tstart, serr := processStartTime(pid)\n   111\t\t\t\tif reviewProcessGoneErr(serr) {\n   112\t\t\t\t\tcontinue\n   113\t\t\t\t}\n   114\t\t\t\tunreadable[pid] = start\n   115\t\t\t\tcontinue\n   116\t\t\tcase !marked:\n   117\t\t\t\tcontinue\n   118\t\t\t}\n   119\t\t\tzombie, err := reviewProcessZombie(pid)\n   120\t\t\tif reviewProcessGoneErr(err) || err == nil && zombie {\n   121\t\t\t\tcontinue\n   122\t\t\t}\n   123\t\t\tif err != nil {\n   124\t\t\t\treturn nil, unreadable, fmt.Errorf(\"process %d state could not be read: %w\", pid, err)\n   125\t\t\t}\n   126\t\t\tout = append(out, pid)\n   127\t\t}\n   128\t\treturn out, unreadable, nil\n   129\t}\n   130\t\n   131\t// killPinnedMarkedProcess signals pid only through a pidfd opened on it,\n   132\t// after the environment read through that same pinned process still holds\n   133\t// entry.\n   134\tfunc killPinnedMarkedProcess(pid int, entry []byte) error {\n   135\t\tfd, err := unix.PidfdOpen(pid, 0)\n   136\t\tif errors.Is(err, unix.ESRCH) {\n   137\t\t\treturn nil\n   138\t\t}\n   139\t\tif err != nil {\n   140\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"process %d could not be pinned: %w\", pid, err)\n   141\t\t}\n   142\t\tdefer unix.Close(fd)\n   143\t\t// The pidfd names one process for its lifetime; if pid was reused before\n   144\t\t// it was opened, the new process does not carry this run's entry.\n   145\t\tmarked, err := reviewProcessMarked(pid, entry)\n   146\t\tif reviewProcessGoneErr(err) || err == nil && !marked {\n   147\t\t\treturn nil\n   148\t\t}\n   149\t\tif err != nil {\n   150\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"process %d could not be inspected: %w\", pid, err)\n   151\t\t}\n   152\t\tif err := unix.PidfdSendSignal(fd, unix.SIGKILL, nil, 0); err != nil && !errors.Is(err, unix.ESRCH) {\n   153\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"process %d could not be ended: %w\", pid, err)\n   154\t\t}\n   155\t\treturn nil\n   156\t}\n   157\t\n   158\tfunc reviewProcessMarked(pid int, entry []byte) (bool, error) {\n   159\t\tenviron, err := os.ReadFile(filepath.Join(\"/proc\", strconv.Itoa(pid), \"environ\"))\n   160\t\tif err != nil {\n   161\t\t\treturn false, err\n   162\t\t}\n   163\t\tfor _, kv := range bytes.Split(environ, []byte{0}) {\n   164\t\t\tif bytes.Equal(kv, entry) {\n   165\t\t\t\treturn true, nil\n   166\t\t\t}\n   167\t\t}\n   168\t\treturn false, nil\n   169\t}\n   170\t\n   171\tfunc reviewProcessOwner(pid int) (int, error) {\n   172\t\tinfo, err := os.Stat(filepath.Join(\"/proc\", strconv.Itoa(pid)))\n   173\t\tif err != nil {\n   174\t\t\treturn 0, err\n   175\t\t}\n   176\t\tst, ok := info.Sys().(*syscall.Stat_t)\n   177\t\tif !ok {\n   178\t\t\treturn 0, fmt.Errorf(\"process %d owner unavailable\", pid)\n   179\t\t}\n   180\t\treturn int(st.Uid), nil\n   181\t}\n   182\t\n   183\tfunc reviewProcessGoneErr(err error) bool {\n   184\t\treturn errors.Is(err, fs.ErrNotExist) || errors.Is(err, syscall.ESRCH)\n   185\t}\n   186\t\n   187\tfunc reviewProcessName(pid int) string {\n   188\t\traw, err := os.ReadFile(filepath.Join(\"/proc\", strconv.Itoa(pid), \"comm\"))\n   189\t\tif err != nil {\n   190\t\t\treturn \"?\"\n   191\t\t}\n   192\t\treturn strings.TrimSpace(string(raw))\n   193\t}\n   194\t\n   195\tfunc reviewProcessZombie(pid int) (bool, error) {\n   196\t\traw, err := os.ReadFile(filepath.Join(\"/proc\", strconv.Itoa(pid), \"stat\"))\n   197\t\tif err != nil {\n   198\t\t\treturn false, err\n   199\t\t}\n   200\t\t// The state follows the parenthesised command name.\n   201\t\tif i := bytes.LastIndexByte(raw, ')'); i >= 0 && i+2 < len(raw) {\n   202\t\t\treturn raw[i+2] == 'Z', nil\n   203\t\t}\n   204\t\treturn false, fmt.Errorf(\"process %d state is unreadable\", pid)\n   205\t}\n   206\t\n   207\t// reviewOpaqueProcessBaseline records, before the adapter starts, the\n   208\t// processes of this user whose environment cannot be read, by pid and start\n   209\t// time: they cannot be the run's.\n   210\tfunc reviewOpaqueProcessBaseline() map[int]string {\n   211\t\t_, opaque, _ := reviewMarkedProcesses([]byte(SealedCheckoutEnv + \"=\\x00\"))\n   212\t\treturn opaque\n   213\t}\n   995\t\t\t\t\t// The reviewer's shell may resolve another `pose` first; the\n   996\t\t\t\t\t// engine that dispatched the run is the one that checks it.\n   997\t\t\t\t\tif self, err := os.Executable(); err == nil {\n   998\t\t\t\t\t\tenv = append(env, ReviewCLIEnv+\"=\"+self)\n   999\t\t\t\t\t}\n  1000\t\t\t\t}\n  1001\t\t\t}\n  1002\t\t}\n  1003\t\tcmd.Env = env\n  1004\t\tcombined := &reviewBoundedCapture{limit: safety.StreamBytes, cancel: cancel}\n  1005\t\tcmd.Stdout, cmd.Stderr = combined, combined\n  1006\t\t// pose delegate watch follows the normalized, redacted events as they come\n  1007\t\t// (spec pose-delegated-review-completion-signal R9); the file goes when\n  1008\t\t// the record is published.\n  1009\t\tsessionPattern := \"\"\n  1010\t\tif plan.Config.Session != nil {\n  1011\t\t\tsessionPattern = plan.Config.Session.Pattern\n  1012\t\t}\n  1013\t\tif live := s.startDelegationLive(run.AttemptID, plan.Config.Events, secrets, sessionPattern, plan.session, safety.StreamBytes); live != nil {\n  1014\t\t\ttee := io.MultiWriter(combined, live)\n  1015\t\t\tcmd.Stdout, cmd.Stderr = tee, tee\n  1016\t\t\tdefer func() { _ = os.Remove(s.delegationLivePath(run.AttemptID)) }()\n  1017\t\t\tdefer live.Close()\n  1018\t\t}\n  1019\t\t// Adapters such as `codex exec` and `claude -p` start children; killing\n  1020\t\t// only the parent left a child holding stdout, so the timeout never fired\n  1021\t\t// (found in review). The run gets its own process group, the whole group\n  1022\t\t// is killed on timeout and after the run, and pipes are released at most\n  1023\t\t// a few seconds after the kill.\n  1024\t\topaqueBaseline := reviewOpaqueProcessBaseline()\n  1025\t\tisolateProcessGroup(cmd)\n  1026\t\tcmd.WaitDelay = AdapterPipeGrace\n  1027\t\tvar runErr error\n  1028\t\tif run.Provenance == nil {\n  1029\t\t\trunErr = cmd.Run()\n  1030\t\t} else {\n  1031\t\t\tdigest, n, complete, started, err := runProvenanceCommand(cmd, plan.Brief.Text)\n  1032\t\t\trunErr = err\n  1033\t\t\trun.Provenance.WireDigest, run.Provenance.WireBytes, run.Provenance.WireComplete = digest, n, complete\n  1034\t\t\tif started {\n  1035\t\t\t\trun.Provenance.ExecutionState = \"started\"\n  1036\t\t\t}\n  1037\t\t}\n  1038\t\tterminationErr = killProcessGroup(cmd)\n  1039\t\t// A command the reviewer left running in a session of its own escapes the\n  1040\t\t// group kill; it is ended here, before the cleanup inventory reads the\n  1041\t\t// directories it may still write (spec\n  1042\t\t// pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes R1, R2).\n  1043\t\treaped, opaque, reapErr := reapSealedCheckoutProcesses(worktree, opaqueBaseline)\n  1044\t\tif reapErr != nil {\n  1045\t\t\tterminationErr = errors.Join(terminationErr, reapErr)\n  1046\t\t}\n  1047\t\tif len(reaped) > 0 && safety != nil {\n  1048\t\t\tsafety.Limitations = append(safety.Limitations, \"ended \"+fmt.Sprint(len(reaped))+\" process(es) the run left running: \"+strings.Join(reaped, \", \"))\n  1049\t\t}\n  1050\t\tif opaque > 0 && safety != nil {\n  1051\t\t\tsafety.Limitations = append(safety.Limitations, fmt.Sprint(opaque)+\" process(es) of this user that existed before the run could not be inspected for its environment entry\")\n  1052\t\t}\n  1053\t\tterminationFailed = terminationErr != nil\n  1054\t\t// The adapter exited and a child it left still held the output when\n  1055\t\t// WaitDelay expired: the run finished, its leftover is killed above, and\n  1056\t\t// the exit status decides (found in review).\n  1057\t\tif errors.Is(runErr, exec.ErrWaitDelay) && cmd.ProcessState != nil && cmd.ProcessState.Success() {\n  1058\t\t\trunErr = nil\n  1059\t\t}\n  1060\t\ttranscript, overflow := combined.result()\n  1061\t\tsafety.CaptureComplete = !overflow\n  1062\t\tif cmd.ProcessState != nil {\n  1063\t\t\trun.ExitCode = cmd.ProcessState.ExitCode()\n  1064\t\t}\n  1065\t\traw, outputErr := readReviewAdapterOutput(runtimeRoot, safety.OutputBytes)\n  1066\t\tif outputErr != nil && !errors.Is(outputErr, os.ErrNotExist) {\n  1067\t\t\tsafety.CaptureComplete = false\n  1068\t\t}\n  1069\t\tif outputErr == nil && len(bytes.TrimSpace(raw)) > 0 {\n  1070\t\t\trun.Output = string(raw)\n  1071\t\t\tif run.Provenance != nil {\n  1072\t\t\t\trun.Provenance.OutputComplete = true\n  1073\t\t\t\trun.Provenance.OutputSource = \"file\"\n  1074\t\t\t}\n  1075\t\t} else if final := DelegationStreamFinal(plan.Config.Events, transcript); strings.TrimSpace(final) != \"\" && int64(len(final)) <= safety.OutputBytes {\n   185\t\told := time.Now().Add(-time.Hour).UTC().Format(time.RFC3339Nano)\n   186\t\tmarker.Owner.PID, marker.HeartbeatAt, marker.StartedAt = dead.Process.Pid, old, old\n   187\t\traw, _ = json.Marshal(marker)\n   188\t\tif err := os.WriteFile(path, raw, 0o600); err != nil {\n   189\t\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n   190\t\t}\n   191\t}\n   192\t\n   193\t// Review round 2, N4 (R6): a real dispatch interrupted after its reservation\n   194\t// and before its run record blocks the next dispatch; once released, the\n   195\t// next dispatch runs.\n   196\tfunc TestAnInterruptedDispatchIsReleasedAndTheNextOneRuns(t *testing.T) {\n   197\t\tf := provenanceRunFixture(t, \"openai\", \"probe-model\")\n   198\t\tplan, err := f.store.PlanReviewDispatch(f.bundle.BundleID, \"review\", \"fixture labelled notes\", \"fake\", \"interrupted\")\n   199\t\tif err != nil {\n   200\t\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n   201\t\t}\n   202\t\tattempt := \"\"\n   203\t\tplan.OnStart = func(a string) error { attempt = a; panic(\"the dispatching process ends here\") }\n   204\t\tfunc() {\n   205\t\t\tdefer func() { _ = recover() }()\n   206\t\t\t_, _ = f.store.RunReviewDispatchContext(context.Background(), plan, time.Now)\n   207\t\t}()\n   208\t\tif attempt == \"\" {\n   209\t\t\tt.Fatal(\"the dispatch never reached its start\")\n   210\t\t}\n   211\t\twriteDeadMarker(t, f.store, attempt)\n   212\t\tif _, err := f.store.PlanReviewDispatch(f.bundle.BundleID, \"review\", \"fixture labelled notes\", \"fake\", \"after interruption\"); err == nil || !strings.Contains(err.Error(), \"pose delegate cancel \"+attempt) {\n   213\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"the interrupted attempt did not block the bundle with its release command: %v\", err)\n   214\t\t}\n   215\t\tif _, err := f.store.ReleaseAbandonedAttempt(attempt, time.Now()); err != nil {\n   216\t\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n   217\t\t}\n   218\t\tnext, err := f.store.PlanReviewDispatch(f.bundle.BundleID, \"review\", \"fixture labelled notes\", \"fake\", \"after release\")\n   219\t\tif err != nil {\n   220\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"the released attempt still blocks the bundle: %v\", err)\n   221\t\t}\n   222\t\tif run, err := f.store.RunReviewDispatchContext(context.Background(), next, time.Now); err != nil || run.Status != ReviewRunCompleted {\n   223\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"the next dispatch did not run: %s %v\", run.Status, err)\n   224\t\t}\n   225\t}\n   226\t\n   227\t// Review round 2, N3: a release already claimed is not run again.\n   228\tfunc TestAClaimedReleaseIsNotRunTwice(t *testing.T) {\n   229\t\troot := t.TempDir()\n   230\t\ts := Store{Root: root}\n   231\t\tattempt := \"rat-\" + strings.Repeat(\"9\", 64)\n   232\t\tdir, _ := s.delegationActiveDir(true)\n   233\t\tif err := os.WriteFile(filepath.Join(dir, attempt+\".release\"), []byte(\"x\\n\"), 0o600); err != nil {\n   234\t\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n   235\t\t}\n   236\t\tif _, err := s.ReleaseAbandonedAttempt(attempt, time.Now()); !errors.Is(err, ErrAttemptNotAbandoned) || !strings.Contains(err.Error(), \"in progress\") {\n   237\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"a claimed release ran again: %v\", err)\n   238\t\t}\n   239\t}\n   240\t\n   241\t// Review round 2, N1: a reservation an earlier engine left with no marker is\n   242\t// listed and released once it is old enough, never while it is young.\n   243\tfunc TestAMarkerlessReservationOfAnEarlierEngineIsReleased(t *testing.T) {\n   244\t\troot := t.TempDir()\n   245\t\ts := Store{Root: root}\n   246\t\treserve := func(age time.Duration, nonce string) DelegatedReviewAttempt {\n   247\t\t\ta := DelegatedReviewAttempt{SchemaVersion: 1, BundleID: \"rvb-00000000000000b\" + nonce[:1], BundleDigest: \"sha256:\" + strings.Repeat(\"a\", 64), Scope: \"spec:alpha\", Adapter: \"fake\", Ordinal: 1,\n   248\t\t\t\tReservedAt: time.Now().Add(-age).UTC().Format(time.RFC3339Nano), Nonce: strings.Repeat(nonce[:1], 32)}\n   249\t\t\ta.AttemptID = attemptIdentity(a)\n   250\t\t\trel, _ := filepath.Rel(root, reviewAttemptPath(root, a))\n   251\t\t\tif err := publishLedgerJSON(root, filepath.ToSlash(rel), a); err != nil {\n   252\t\t\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n   253\t\t\t}\n   254\t\t\treturn a\n   255\t\t}\n   256\t\told, young := reserve(time.Hour, \"1\"), reserve(time.Minute, \"2\")\n   257\t\tattempts, _, err := s.ListDelegationAttempts()\n   258\t\tif err != nil {\n   259\t\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n   260\t\t}\n   261\t\tlisted := map[string]DelegationAttempt{}\n   262\t\tfor _, a := range attempts {\n   263\t\t\tlisted[a.AttemptID] = a\n   264\t\t}\n   265\t\tif a, ok := listed[old.AttemptID]; !ok || a.State != DelegationStalled || !strings.Contains(a.Failure, \"pose delegate cancel \"+old.AttemptID) {\n   266\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"the old markerless reservation is not listed with its release: %+v\", attempts)\n   267\t\t}\n   268\t\tif _, ok := listed[young.AttemptID]; ok {\n   269\t\t\tt.Fatal(\"a young reservation was listed as abandoned\")\n   270\t\t}\n   271\t\tif _, err := s.ReleaseAbandonedAttempt(young.AttemptID, time.Now()); !errors.Is(err, ErrAttemptNotAbandoned) {\n   272\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"a young reservation was released: %v\", err)\n   273\t\t}\n   274\t\trun, err := s.ReleaseAbandonedAttempt(old.AttemptID, time.Now())\n   275\t\tif err != nil || run.Status != ReviewRunFailed || !strings.Contains(run.Failure, \"earlier engine\") {\n   276\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"release: %+v %v\", run, err)\n   277\t\t}\n   278\t\tif _, err := s.readAttemptReceipt(old); err != nil {\n   279\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"the released reservation still blocks its bundle: %v\", err)\n   280\t\t}\n   281\t}\n  1110\tfunc cmdDelegateCancel(root string, args []string, stdout, stderr io.Writer) int {\n  1111\t\tf, problem := parseDelegateFlags(args)\n  1112\t\tif problem != \"\" {\n  1113\t\t\treturn delegateUsage(stdout, stderr, args, \"cancel\", problem+\"\\n\"+tr(\"Usage: \", \"Uso: \")+\"pose delegate cancel <run> [--dry-run] [--json]\")\n  1114\t\t}\n  1115\t\tstore := posemodel.Store{Root: root}\n  1116\t\tattempts, lost, err := store.ListDelegationAttempts()\n  1117\t\tif err != nil {\n  1118\t\t\treturn delegateFail(stdout, stderr, f.jsonOut, \"cancel\", 1, err)\n  1119\t\t}\n  1120\t\tattempt, code, err := namedAttempt(attempts, f)\n  1121\t\tif err != nil {\n  1122\t\t\treturn delegateFail(stdout, stderr, f.jsonOut, \"cancel\", code, withDelegationLosses(err, lost))\n  1123\t\t}\n  1124\t\tif attempt.State == posemodel.DelegationStalled && attempt.LatestRun == \"\" && !f.dryRun {\n  1125\t\t\t// An attempt whose dispatch ended before recording its run is\n  1126\t\t\t// released with a failed run and its receipt, so it stops blocking\n  1127\t\t\t// the bundle (spec pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes R5).\n  1128\t\t\trun, err := store.ReleaseAbandonedAttempt(attempt.AttemptID, time.Now())\n  1129\t\t\tif err != nil {\n  1130\t\t\t\treturn delegateFail(stdout, stderr, f.jsonOut, \"cancel\", 1, err)\n  1131\t\t\t}\n  1132\t\t\tif f.jsonOut {\n  1133\t\t\t\twriteDelegateJSON(stdout, map[string]any{\"schema\": delegateCancelSchema, \"attempt\": attempt.AttemptID, \"released\": true, \"run\": run.RunID, \"status\": run.Status})\n  1134\t\t\t\treturn 0\n  1135\t\t\t}\n  1136\t\t\tout := render(stdout, stderr)\n  1137\t\t\tout.Field(\"delegate.attempt\", attempt.AttemptID)\n  1138\t\t\tif run.RunID == \"\" {\n  1139\t\t\t\tout.Field(\"delegate.released\", tr(\"true: no reservation was published; the stalled marker was removed\", \"true: nenhuma reserva foi publicada; o marcador parado foi removido\"))\n  1140\t\t\t} else {\n  1141\t\t\t\tout.Field(\"delegate.released\", tr(\"true: recorded as failed run \"+run.RunID+\" (abandoned before its run was recorded)\", \"true: registrada como run com falha \"+run.RunID+\" (abandonada antes de o run ser registrado)\"))\n  1142\t\t\t}\n  1143\t\t\treturn 0\n  1144\t\t}\n  1145\t\tif !attempt.Active {\n  1146\t\t\treturn delegateFail(stdout, stderr, f.jsonOut, \"cancel\", 1, withDelegationLosses(errors.New(tr(\"attempt \"+attempt.AttemptID+\" is \"+attempt.State+\", not running\",\n  1147\t\t\t\t\"a tentativa \"+attempt.AttemptID+\" está \"+attempt.State+\", não rodando\")), lost))\n  1148\t\t}\n  1149\t\tif f.dryRun {\n  1150\t\t\tif f.jsonOut {\n  1151\t\t\t\twriteDelegateJSON(stdout, map[string]any{\"schema\": delegateCancelSchema, \"attempt\": attempt.AttemptID, \"requested\": false, \"dry_run\": true, \"owner\": attempt.Liveness})\n  1152\t\t\t\treturn 0\n  1153\t\t\t}\n  1154\t\t\tout := render(stdout, stderr)\n  1155\t\t\tout.Field(\"delegate.attempt\", attempt.AttemptID)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
