ould not be read (one started during the run that cannot be read fails the cleanup); on other platforms only the process group is ended; the brief of template `review-brief/10` asks the reviewer to let its commands finish. The dispatch marks an attempt active before it publishes its reservation, so a dispatch that ends before recording its run always leaves a stalled attempt, which `pose delegate ls` lists with its cause, as it does a reservation an earlier engine left without a marker once it is ten minutes old; `pose delegate cancel <attempt>` releases it once its owner is proven gone, recording a failed run and its receipt.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
